diff --git a/docs/boot.md b/docs/boot.md
index 7ec69f0314934c05c62ba643d46a5a98f7af1161..6e051b9129036d74edfc9151e88d0c00697ff8eb 100644
--- a/docs/boot.md
+++ b/docs/boot.md
@@ -28,8 +28,15 @@ Two traces are written independently:
 
 `tools/boot_trace.py` reads both and prints the triage units: modules, unimplemented calls and callers,
 DllMain/TLS results, exceptions with their stack frames, the exit, and the D3D12 calls by outcome and first call
-per method. The `[rt]` lines in the same stderr log carry the device parameters, feature ids and warnings; the
-summary leaves them as a count, so grep `^\[rt\]` for those.
+per method. The same report counts shader translation lookup failures by stage. For builds with
+`LEONIDA_STUB_PIPELINES`, the highest logged creation milestone gives a lower bound on stub pipelines created.
+The runtime can create a pipeline without ever drawing with it.
+
+If the presenter logged capture measurements, the report counts black and nonblack readbacks.
+On older builds, a positive mean establishes color, while three rounded zero means leave the capture
+inconclusive. A successful `PresentX` call alone gives no pixel measurement. To share just the counters,
+run `python -I tools/boot_trace.py --d3d12 d3d12.log --counts-only`. For device parameters, feature IDs
+and other warnings, inspect the original stderr locally.
 
 ## 2. Commands
 
